{
  "dom_id": "question-331821",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "Consider a function $b(t)$ such that its Laplace transform is $L\\{b(t)\\}=B(s)$ for $s>{s}_{0}.$ Suppose we wish to find $L\\{{e}^{t}b(t)\\}.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nBy definition of the Laplace transform, we can write \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L\\{{e}^{t}b(t)\\} & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{{field-1}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{{field-2}}\\,b(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={{field-3}}\\,\\text{for}\\,{{field-4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [
    {
      "key": "field-1",
      "type": "select",
